---
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';
import Prose from '../components/Prose.astro';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Trademark · TachyonCMS"
  description="How you can use the TachyonCMS name and logo: freely to talk about the project, never in a way that makes your thing look like ours."
  path="/trademark"
>
  <PageHero
    eyebrow="Trademark"
    title="Use the name to talk about us, not to be us"
    lede="The code is yours under the MIT License. The name and the logo are how people know what's really TachyonCMS, so they come with a few plain rules."
  >
    <p class="notice">Last updated <time datetime="2026-10-28">28 October 2026</time>.</p>
  </PageHero>

  <div class="trademark">
    <Prose>
      <h2>What's covered</h2>
      <p>
        The name <strong>TachyonCMS</strong>, and the logo and mark you can download from the{' '}
        <a href="/brand">brand page</a>. The MIT License covers the code. It doesn't cover the name or the logo, which is
        why this page exists.
      </p>
      <p>
        For now I look after them. Once TachyonCMS has maintainers from more than one organization, the plan in{' '}
        <a href="https://github.com/tachyon-cms/tachyoncms/blob/main/GOVERNANCE.md">GOVERNANCE.md</a> is to move the project,
        its trademark and its domains to a neutral foundation.
      </p>

      <h2>Go ahead, no need to ask</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Write, post, talk or teach about TachyonCMS, and use the logo to illustrate it.</li>
        <li>Say your site, plugin, starter or service works with TachyonCMS or is built on it.</li>
        <li>Link to tachyoncms.com or the repository with the logo or the mark.</li>
        <li>Run it, modify it and fork it, for anything, as the MIT License allows.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Please don't</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          Name your product, service, company or domain so it looks like TachyonCMS itself: "TachyonCMS Cloud", say, or
          tachyoncms-hosting.com.
        </li>
        <li>Suggest the project endorses, sponsors or runs your thing when it doesn't.</li>
        <li>Ship a modified version under the TachyonCMS name. Forks are welcome; give yours a name of its own.</li>
        <li>Change the logo's colours or shape, or blend it into your own logo.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Not sure?</h2>
      <p>
        Ask at <a href="mailto:legal@tachyoncms.com">legal@tachyoncms.com</a>. Most answers will be yes, and a quick email
        now beats a rename later.
      </p>
    </Prose>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .trademark {
    padding-bottom: clamp(3rem, 8vw, 5rem);
  }
  .trademark :global(.prose h2:first-child) {
    margin-top: 0;
  }
</style>
